#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# spheroidal_s1

#% text
# `spheroidal_s1(n, m, gamma, z)` gives the radial spheroidal function of the first kind `S^(m)(1)_n(z, gamma)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The function is the expansion `(z^2 - 1)^(m/2) z^(-m) sum a_k w_k j_(n+2k)(gamma z)/sum (-1)^k a_k w_k` in spherical Bessel functions, with the coefficients `a_k` of `spheroidal_ps` and `w_k = (n + m + 2k)!/(n - m + 2k)!` (Flammer 1957, 4.1.17; DLMF 30.11.3).

#% item
# Integers `n >= m >= 0` and inexact `gamma` or `z` (exact arguments stay unevaluated); the value is complex, with an inexact zero imaginary part when it is real. Arguments with more digits give a value of that precision.

#% item
# `spheroidal_s1` threads over lists of `z`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
spheroidal_s1(1, 0, 2.5, 1)
#% output
#= 0.584507273003611 + 0.0im

#% cell
spheroidal_s1(5, 1, 0.1, 0.3)
#% output
#= -0.0 - 3.934705565821266e-12im

#% cell
n(spheroidal_s1(7, 5, 1, 2), 30)
#% output
#= 0.00002738983051767685078038275244168 + 0.im

#% cell
n(spheroidal_s1(2, 1, 1/3, -11), 20)
#% output
#= -0.29985857194498797329 + 0.im

#% text
# A list of arguments, one of them large:

#% cell
spheroidal_s1(1, 0, 1.5, [0.5, 2.0, 200.0])
#% output
#= [0.2597690237629468 + 0.0im, 0.3949083238478165 + 0.0im, 6.774300789537011e-5 + 0.0im]

#% text
# The derivative in `z` is `spheroidal_s1_prime`:

#% cell
d(spheroidal_s1(2, 1, 1.3, z), z)
#% output
#= spheroidal_s1_prime(2, 1, 1.3, z)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `spheroidal_ps`, `spheroidal_eigenvalue`, `spherical_bessel_j`, `spheroidal_s1_prime`
